 BYPASSED never converts ACTIVE to INACTIVE. A known PROXY self-call inherits
 the caller's P (or its known absence/uncertainty), ignoring the called annotation's
-propagation. UNKNOWN advice produces UNKNOWN effective context and stops confident
-body traversal. An unannotated wrapper can retain a known initial context while a
-later annotated call becomes UNKNOWN; its subsequent continuation is then UNKNOWN.
+propagation. F02 composes APPLIED and BYPASSED when advice application is the only
